Same issue as the v1 hook, and v2 is the version where it bites hardest.

v2.8.0's `options.Client()` does `opts.SetHTTPClient(httputil.NewHTTPClient())`, so
each call allocates a *fresh* `http.Client`. Being last in the merge, this element's
client wins over anything the caller configured on an earlier element. v2's
`MergeClientOptions` uses reflection over exported fields with `!field.IsZero()`, so
the non-zero `HTTPClient` is copied over just like any other field.

